 goods (dairy, meat, and fisheries) exported from a country over a specific period.^India exports 40% of the Agricultural & Allied Products to Asia, while the US's share is the highest (~17%) amongst countries."},{"question":"What is the significance of the Exports - Agricultural & Allied Products data?","answer":"Agricultural exports contribute significantly to a country's economy, bringing in foreign exchange and enhancing the importance of the agriculture sector.^This data is crucial for understanding the global demand for India's agricultural products and the sector's contribution to the national economy.^It reflects the competitiveness, quality, and diversity of agricultural products in the international market. A wide range of exported products indicates a robust and diverse agricultural sector.^Global demand patterns for specific agricultural products can guide production and marketing strategies and also to balance the internal and external demand for agricultural products.^The volume and value of exports can be influenced by trade policies, international agreements, and tariffs, making this data crucial for necessary policy formulation."},{"question":"How to interpret the Exports - Agricultural & Allied Products data?","answer":"Higher exports reflect surplus domestic production and also rising demand from the importing countries.^High export volumes can lead to increased incomes for farmers and provide incentives for adopting improved agricultural practices.^Historical trends in agricultural exports help to analyse changes in global demand, market preferences, and the competitive position of the country's agricultural sector.^The impact of external factors such as global market conditions, trade policies, currency exchange rates, and international trade agreements on agricultural exports.^Higher exports despite high domestic consumption may lead to higher inflation in those commodities."}],"related":[{"slug":"annual-rainfall-lpa","title":"Annual Rainfall (% of LPA)"},{"slug":"consumer-price-index-cpi-inflation-food","title":"Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation - Food"},{"slug":"consumer-price-index-cpi-inflation-food-rural","title":"Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation - Food Rural"},{"slug":"consumer-price-index-cpi-inflation-miscellaneous-rural","title":"Consumer Price Index (CPI) Inflation- Miscellaneous Rural"},{"slug":"domestic-tractor-sales","title":"Domestic Tractor Sales"},{"slug":"fertiliser-sales","title":"Fertiliser Sales"},{"slug":"foodgrain-stocks","title":"Foodgrain Stocks"},{"slug":"kharif-sowing-progress","title":"Kharif Sowing Progress"},{"slug":"rabi-sowing-progress","title":"Rabi Sowing Progress"},{"slug":"reservoir-level-10-year-average","title":"Reservoir Level (vs 10Y Avg)"},{"slug":"south-west-monsoon-rainfall-deviation-from-normal","title":"South-west Monsoon Rainfall: Deviation from Normal"},{"slug":"wholesale-price-index-wpi-inflation-food","title":"Wholesale Price Index (WPI) Inflation - Food"}],"title":"Exports - Agricultural & Allied Products","description":"Agricultural and allied product exports stand at $ 4,313.9 Million for Aug 2026. This category is exposed to global commodity prices and domestic export policy.","headline":{"Absolute":"Agricultural and allied product exports stand at $ 4,313.9 Million for Aug 2026. This category is exposed to global commodity prices and domestic export policy.","Y-o-Y":"Agricultural and allied product exports stand at 4.58% for Aug 2026. This category is exposed to global commodity prices and domestic export policy."},"source":null,"source_url":null,"date_modified":"2026-08-01","scraped_at":"2026-10-30T06:10:50+00:00"}